{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216833-list-of-spirits","id":1216833,"title":"List of Spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-08T15:42:35-07:00","id":1216833,"title":"List of Spirits?","content":"I'm gonna be playing an Urban Shaman in a game pretty soon, lots of Spirit and Prime is my goal, but my ST has never really dealt with someone who primarily binds, bargains, summons etc.<br /> <br /> I know that Spirit and Prime are pretty ST heavy Spheres, and I was wondering if there was a good resource for different spirits in the books so that we could have something to draw off of.<br /> <br /> I know that in the M20 Core Book they have the hierarchy of Umbral Entities and Miscellaneous Entities, and then the list of charms and the mechanics of gnosis, rage and willpower, etc. but I can't seem to find any examples of Spirits with stats included. And I know the book of secrets talks all about how to work with and ward against spirits and stuff.<br /> <br /> Am I not looking hard enough? Should I be looking more at Werewolf, maybe?<br /> <br /> Any help is appreciated!<br /> <br /> Edit: the how to do that book has the spirit summoning rules, not the book of secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24199-tigerman","user":"Tigerman","date":". 05-08-2018, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24199-tigerman","name":"Tigerman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:25:05-07:00","id":1216844,"title":"","content":"Book of Madness, Book of Worlds, Spirit Ways and some Werewolf books like Axis Mundi and Velvet Shadows would probably be the most useful.<br /> <br /> I'd also read books on folklore and such depending on the local and the culture(s) of your character. My games had several characters that were shaman-type mages, and those were very helpful in giving spirits a personal touch and reflecting how the characters specifically viewed and interacted with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 05-08-2018, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:26:00-07:00","id":1216845,"title":"","content":"Axis Mundi, which is a Mage and Werewolf book, has spirits. You also have some rules on shamanism in Spirit Ways. Some parts of the various books on the Umbra, such as Beyond The Barriers: The Book of Worlds and the Infinite Tapestry might prove useful.<br /> <br /> Werewolf probably has quite a few books other than Axis Mundi which cover spirits, but I've not read enough of the other books to know how useful they are.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers in Werewolf are the urban shamans tribe specializing in spirit magic, so there might be inspiration from that tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:27:37-07:00","id":1216846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216833-list-of-spirits?p=1216845#post1216845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Glass Walkers in Werewolf are the urban shamans tribe specializing in spirit magic, so there might be inspiration from that tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Bone Gnawers for dealing with urban spirits of more 'low places'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:53:52-07:00","id":1216853,"title":"","content":"To that end, focusing on the totem spirits of Rat and Cockroach, as well as their respective broods would probably be a good place to start. And depending on whether or not your character does tech stuff, book of the Weaver could also offer some interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, I\u2019d say you would probably get a lot out of it if you think about what spiritual beliefs your urban shaman had. Whether there\u2019s a particular mythology or pantheon of god\u2019s they adhere to, or if it\u2019s a bit more slap dash than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:55:54-07:00","id":1216855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tigerman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216833-list-of-spirits#post1216833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be playing an Urban Shaman in a game pretty soon, lots of Spirit and Prime is my goal, but my ST has never really dealt with someone who primarily binds, bargains, summons etc.<br /> <br /> I know that Spirit and Prime are pretty ST heavy Spheres, and I was wondering if there was a good resource for different spirits in the books so that we could have something to draw off of.<br /> <br /> I know that in the M20 Core Book they have the hierarchy of Umbral Entities and Miscellaneous Entities, and then the list of charms and the mechanics of gnosis, rage and willpower, etc. but I can't seem to find any examples of Spirits with stats included. And I know the book of secrets talks all about how to work with and ward against spirits and stuff.<br /> <br /> Am I not looking hard enough? Should I be looking more at Werewolf, maybe?<br /> <br /> Any help is appreciated!<br /> <br /> Edit: the how to do that book has the spirit summoning rules, not the book of secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to M20, p.633. Examples of many totem spirits and elementals, along with others, are given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T23:51:29-07:00","id":1377463,"title":"","content":"Spirits by Type: <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf</a><br /> Totems by Type: <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/totems.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/totems.pdf</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:39:45-07:00","id":1377490,"title":"","content":"Axis Mundi, the Book of Spirits. Pretty helpful, exactly what you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:36:37-07:00","id":1377507,"title":"","content":"Book of Mirrors and Book of Madness have very interesting spirits as well. Book of Mirrors even has something that is said to be on the level of an Incarna, manifesting as a Death Epiphling who is...well, Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:32:13-07:00","id":1378108,"title":"","content":"I liked the chats that i found (I wish i had made the them) they show the book and where they are all mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}